{"id":"standing_cable_abduction","name":"Standing cable abduction","cue":"Stand tall and lift the leg out to the side.","research":"Standing cable hip abduction, right leg working, the column on the left. Design values from the standard technique description, not a measured trial: standing tall on the left leg (knee 3, the sole flat on the plate), the left hand on a vertical grab bar of the column (arm nearly straight, hand 0.32 H out), the right hand resting at the hip, the trunk leaning 4 deg toward the standing side and the pelvis kept level. A cuff on the right ankle (0.07 to 0.11 H above the floor) carries a ring on its inner side; the cable runs from the low pulley (0.075 H, 0.08 H out from the column toward the lifter and 0.24 H ahead of the stance) across the front of the standing shank to the ring, so it pulls the ankle in and forward and the leg is lifted out and away against it. The working leg goes from 3 deg of hip abduction (the foot beside the other, just off the plate, hip flexion 4, knee 6) to 36 deg (research range 45; the rig limit is 45), the foot 0.35 H out and 0.11 H up, toes forward, the pelvis not hiking. Cable 1:1 to the stack. Geometry: design/cable/ab.mjs.","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"hip_abduction_r":3,"hip_flexion_r":4,"knee_flexion_r":6,"knee_flexion_l":3},"B":{"hip_abduction_r":36,"hip_flexion_r":4,"knee_flexion_r":6},"note":"design values (standard technique), not a measured trial"},"muscles":{"primary":["glute_med","glute_max_up"],"secondary":[],"side":"r"},"camera":{"az":150,"el":15,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.6,"note":"From behind and to the right (az 150, el 15, 30 deg off the view from behind): the right upper glute faces the camera and the leg opening out to the right shows its whole sweep; the column stands on the far side and its grab bar and the cable to the cuff stay in view. The standing leg and the working leg do not overlap at the finish."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"mirror":false,"tempo":[1,0.5,2.5,0.5],"root":[-0.05,0.53,0],"